QEMU 11.1.1 linux-user: never wait for mmap_lock inside an RCU read section.

paslang's arm64 tests run under QEMU's user mode, built from the signed
11.1.1 release with this patch (scripts/build_qemu.py). A guest that
forks while another of its threads makes a system call with a pointer
deadlocks (paslang P226, found on testdata/sysprocesses: 19 hangs in
240 runs):

- page_check_range() (accel/tcg/user-exec.c) looks a range up under
  RCU_READ_LOCK_GUARD() and, on a miss of the lockless lookup or to
  call page_unprotect(), takes mmap_lock() inside that read section;
- fork_start() (linux-user/main.c) holds mmap_lock while fork() runs
  util/rcu.c's atfork handler, rcu_init_lock(), which waits for
  rcu_sync_lock;
- synchronize_rcu() holds rcu_sync_lock while wait_for_readers() waits
  for the reader of the first point.

The reader leaves the read section before it waits for mmap_lock and
looks again with the lock held, as the original does after a miss;
pageflags_find() under mmap_lock needs no read section. With it,
sysprocesses ran 400 times without a hang. QEMU's master branch has the
same code.

--- a/accel/tcg/user-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/user-exec.c
@@ -508,7 +508,12 @@
         return false; /* wrap around */
     }
 
-    RCU_READ_LOCK_GUARD();
+    /*
+     * mmap_lock is never waited for inside the RCU read side: fork_start()
+     * holds it while fork()'s RCU atfork handler waits for rcu_sync_lock,
+     * which synchronize_rcu() holds while it waits for this reader.
+     */
+    rcu_read_lock();
 
     locked = have_mmap_lock();
     while (true) {
@@ -521,7 +526,9 @@
                  * Lockless lookups have false negatives.
                  * Retry with the lock held.
                  */
+                rcu_read_unlock();
                 mmap_lock();
+                rcu_read_lock();
                 locked = -1;
                 p = pageflags_find(start, last);
             }
@@ -545,6 +552,14 @@
                 ret = false; /* page not writable */
                 break;
             }
+            /* page_unprotect() takes mmap_lock: take it outside first. */
+            if (!locked) {
+                rcu_read_unlock();
+                mmap_lock();
+                rcu_read_lock();
+                locked = -1;
+                continue;
+            }
             /* Asking about writable, but has been protected: undo. */
             if (!page_unprotect(NULL, start, 0)) {
                 ret = false;
@@ -566,6 +581,7 @@
         start = p->itree.last + 1;
     }
 
+    rcu_read_unlock();
     /* Release the lock if acquired locally. */
     if (locked < 0) {
         mmap_unlock();
